    "text": "A high-bar back squatter with disproportionately long femurs relative to torso length shows a pronounced forward trunk lean and slight heel rise at the bottom of the squat. A weight-bearing ankle dorsiflexion lunge test scores within normal limits (greater than 10 cm) bilaterally, a passive hip flexion screen is normal, and the bar path remains vertical over midfoot throughout. Which conclusion and adjustment is best supported?",
