    "section": "practical-applied",
    "domain": "Exercise Technique",
    "topic": "Olympic Lift Derivatives",
    "cognitiveLevel": "Analysis",
    "text": "An athlete's barbell high pull is filmed from the side. During the second pull the hips and knees extend forcefully and the bar reaches an appropriate height near the lower sternum, but throughout the pull the elbows remain below the level of the bar and drive backward rather than out and up, giving the pull the appearance of a heavy upright row. Which correction most directly addresses the cause of this pattern?",
