        "letter": "A",
        "text": "The assistant coach is correct in general principle but wrong about this specific load; because the power pull removes the catch requirement, loads modestly above the competition lift (commonly cited around 100 to 110% of the athlete's clean or snatch 1RM) are an accepted way to overload the pull without asking the athlete to receive an unmakeable weight, provided bar speed and pulling mechanics remain the training priority"
