    "topic": "Speed & Agility",
    "cognitiveLevel": "Analysis",
    "text": "Video analysis of a 505 change-of-direction test shows an athlete reaching the plant step at high approach velocity with good acceleration mechanics, but on the plant/cut step the trunk collapses laterally and the knee moves into valgus, a pattern absent when the same athlete performs the identical cut at roughly 70% approach speed. Which training emphasis is most directly indicated?",
